      "content": "A **for loop** iterates through every element in a **sequence** like a list or string, executing the **loop body** repeatedly until the **iteration** completes. Inside the **loop body**, you can use a **conditional** statement to check if a specific item meets a requirement before processing it. To control the flow, use **range()** to generate a sequence of numbers, and manually **increment** or **decrement** a variable to manage the **iteration** count in a **while loop**. If the **conditional** never becomes false, you risk creating an **infinite loop**, so always ensure termination logic exists. Use **break** to exit the **loop body** immediately when a condition is met, or **continue** to skip the current **iteration** and jump to the next item in the **sequence**. You can also create a **nested loop** by placing a **for loop** or **while loop** inside another **loop body** to process multi-dimensional data. This combination of a **for loop**, **while loop**, **iteration**, **range()**, **increment**, **decrement**, **loop body**, **sequence**, **conditional**, **infinite loop**, **break**, **continue**, and",
